#. help.theme
msgctxt "help.theme"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor theme <command>\n"
"\n"
"  list [--json]             installed themes\n"
"  current                   active theme\n"
"  apply <name>              apply a theme\n"
"  undo                      go back to the previous theme\n"
"  install <path> [--force]  install from a folder or .tar.gz\n"
"  export <name>             pack a theme into <name>.maxortheme\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor theme apply maxor-dark\n"
"    maxor theme undo\n"
"    maxor theme list --json"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor theme <commande>\n"
"\n"
"  list [--json]             thèmes installés\n"
"  current                   thème actif\n"
"  apply <nom>               applique un thème\n"
"  undo                      revient au thème précédent\n"
"  install <chemin> [--force]  installe depuis un dossier ou un .tar.gz\n"
"  export <nom>              empaquette un thème dans <nom>.maxortheme\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor theme apply maxor-dark\n"
"    maxor theme undo\n"
"    maxor theme list --json"

#. help.search
msgctxt "help.search"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor search [text] [--json] [--list]\n"
"\n"
"  In a terminal, with the full-screen app installed, it opens the Store\n"
"  (mark apps, install them, see details). With --list, --json or without\n"
"  a terminal it prints the results as a list.\n"
"\n"
"  --json    print JSON and nothing else\n"
"  --list    print the list instead of opening the Store\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor search brave\n"
"    maxor search --list firefox"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor search [texte] [--json] [--list]\n"
"\n"
"  Dans un terminal, avec l'application plein écran installée, ouvre la Boutique\n"
"  (cochez des applications, installez-les, voyez les détails). Avec --list, --json ou sans\n"
"  terminal, affiche les résultats sous forme de liste.\n"
"\n"
"  --json    affiche du JSON et rien d'autre\n"
"  --list    affiche la liste au lieu d'ouvrir la Boutique\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor search brave\n"
"    maxor search --list firefox"

#. help.install
msgctxt "help.install"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor install <app...> [--nix|--flatpak] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Installs without sudo or rebuild. An id with dots (org.mozilla.firefox)\n"
"  is Flatpak; any other name is nixpkgs. Force the source with the flags.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor install btop\n"
"    maxor install org.mozilla.firefox\n"
"    maxor install --nix vlc"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor install <app...> [--nix|--flatpak] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Installe sans sudo ni reconstruction. Un identifiant avec des points (org.mozilla.firefox)\n"
"  est un Flatpak ; tout autre nom vient de nixpkgs. Forcez la source avec les options.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor install btop\n"
"    maxor install org.mozilla.firefox\n"
"    maxor install --nix vlc"

#. help.remove
msgctxt "help.remove"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor remove <app...> [--purge] [--list-data] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Removes apps installed with maxor. Folders the app left in your home\n"
"  (named exactly like the app) are listed; --purge deletes them too, and\n"
"  also cleans up after an app that is already gone. --list-data only lists them.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor remove btop\n"
"    maxor remove atlauncher --purge"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor remove <app...> [--purge] [--list-data] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Supprime les applications installées avec maxor. Les dossiers que l'application a laissés\n"
"  dans votre dossier personnel (portant exactement son nom) sont listés ; --purge les supprime aussi,\n"
"  et nettoie après une application déjà disparue. --list-data les liste seulement.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor remove btop\n"
"    maxor remove atlauncher --purge"

#. help.apps
msgctxt "help.apps"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor apps [list [--json] | updates | update [app...] | open <app> | repair]\n"
"\n"
"  list      installed apps (default)\n"
"  updates   apps that have a newer version (--refresh to look again, --notify to tell you)\n"
"  update    update every app, or just the ones you name\n"
"  open      open an installed app\n"
"  repair    show Flatpak apps in the app menu and the terminal\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor apps\n"
"    maxor apps updates\n"
"    maxor apps update btop\n"
"    maxor apps open brave"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor apps [list [--json] | updates | update [app...] | open <app> | repair]\n"
"\n"
"  list      applications installées (par défaut)\n"
"  updates   applications ayant une version plus récente (--refresh pour revérifier, --notify pour vous prévenir)\n"
"  update    met à jour toutes les applications, ou seulement celles que vous nommez\n"
"  open      ouvre une application installée\n"
"  repair    affiche les applications Flatpak dans le menu et le terminal\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor apps\n"
"    maxor apps updates\n"
"    maxor apps update btop\n"
"    maxor apps open brave"

#. help.update
msgctxt "help.update"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor update [-y] [--no-lock] [--check] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Updates the flake inputs, builds the system without applying it, shows\n"
"  what changes and asks before switching.\n"
"\n"
"  -y, --yes   apply without asking\n"
"  --no-lock   do not update flake.lock\n"
"  --check     stop after showing the changes\n"
"  --json      same check, as JSON and nothing else (implies --check)\n"
"  --status    JSON: branch of the configuration, nixpkgs channel and generation (instant)\n"
"  --cached    JSON: the last saved check, or null\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor update\n"
"    maxor update --no-lock -y"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor update [-y] [--no-lock] [--check] [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Met à jour les entrées du flake, construit le système sans l'appliquer, montre\n"
"  ce qui change et demande avant de basculer.\n"
"\n"
"  -y, --yes   applique sans demander\n"
"  --no-lock   ne met pas à jour flake.lock\n"
"  --check     s'arrête après avoir montré les changements\n"
"  --json      la même vérification, en JSON et rien d'autre (implique --check)\n"
"  --status    JSON : branche de la configuration, canal nixpkgs et génération (instantané)\n"
"  --cached    JSON : la dernière vérification enregistrée, ou null\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor update\n"
"    maxor update --no-lock -y"

#. help.rollback
msgctxt "help.rollback"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor rollback [N] [-y] | --list [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Goes back to the previous generation, or to generation N.\n"
"  --list shows the latest generations (--json for programs).\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor rollback --list\n"
"    maxor rollback 33"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor rollback [N] [-y] | --list [--json]\n"
"\n"
"  Revient à la génération précédente, ou à la génération N.\n"
"  --list montre les dernières générations (--json pour les programmes).\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor rollback --list\n"
"    maxor rollback 33"

#. help.doctor
msgctxt "help.doctor"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor doctor\n"
"\n"
"  Checks system, session, graphics, boot, identity and configuration.\n"
"  Exit code 1 if something is wrong.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor doctor\n"
"    maxor doctor --json | jq .groups"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor doctor\n"
"\n"
"  Vérifie le système, la session, les graphismes, le démarrage, l'identité et la configuration.\n"
"  Code de sortie 1 si quelque chose ne va pas.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor doctor\n"
"    maxor doctor --json | jq .groups"

#. help.hardware
msgctxt "help.hardware"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor hardware [show | detect [--write [path]]]\n"
"\n"
"  show      detected machine and the drivers Maxor uses (default)\n"
"  detect    print hardware.json; --write saves it for this machine\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor hardware\n"
"    maxor hardware detect --write"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor hardware [show | detect [--write [chemin]]]\n"
"\n"
"  show      l'ordinateur détecté et les pilotes qu'utilise Maxor (par défaut)\n"
"  detect    affiche hardware.json ; --write l'enregistre pour cet ordinateur\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor hardware\n"
"    maxor hardware detect --write"

#. help.profile
msgctxt "help.profile"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor profile [list [--json] | enable <name> [-y|--no-apply] | disable <name> [-y|--no-apply]]\n"
"\n"
"  Profiles: gaming, dev, creator, office.\n"
"  --no-apply   only save the choice; apply it later with maxor update\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor profile enable gaming\n"
"    maxor profile disable dev --no-apply"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor profile [list [--json] | enable <nom> [-y|--no-apply] | disable <nom> [-y|--no-apply]]\n"
"\n"
"  Profils : gaming, dev, creator, office.\n"
"  --no-apply   enregistre seulement le choix ; appliquez-le plus tard avec maxor update\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor profile enable gaming\n"
"    maxor profile disable dev --no-apply"

#. help.ui
msgctxt "help.ui"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor ui [home|store|themes|update|doctor|profiles]\n"
"\n"
"  Opens the full-screen app on that screen (home by default).\n"
"  It takes over your terminal and gives it back, with a short summary,\n"
"  when you quit. Running maxor with no arguments does the same.\n"
"  MAXOR_NO_TUI=1 disables that.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor\n"
"    maxor ui store"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor ui [home|store|themes|update|doctor|profiles]\n"
"\n"
"  Ouvre l'application plein écran sur cet écran (home par défaut).\n"
"  Elle prend votre terminal et le rend, avec un court résumé, quand vous quittez.\n"
"  Lancer maxor sans argument fait la même chose. MAXOR_NO_TUI=1 le désactive.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor\n"
"    maxor ui store"

#. help.setup
msgctxt "help.setup"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor setup\n"
"\n"
"  Opens the setup assistant: pick a look, choose profiles and review\n"
"  what was detected. Safe to run again any time.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor setup"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor setup\n"
"\n"
"  Ouvre l'assistant de configuration : choisissez une apparence, des profils et passez en revue\n"
"  ce qui a été détecté. Peut être relancé à tout moment.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor setup"

#. help.backup
msgctxt "help.backup"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor backup [file] [--json] | --list <file>\n"
"\n"
"  Saves what is yours in one .tar.gz: the active profiles, your own themes,\n"
"  the DankMaterialShell settings and the list of installed apps.\n"
"  hardware.json is not included: each computer detects its own.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor backup\n"
"    maxor backup ~/Documents\n"
"    maxor backup --list copia.tar.gz"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor backup [fichier] [--json] | --list <fichier>\n"
"\n"
"  Sauvegarde ce qui est à vous dans un .tar.gz : les profils actifs, vos propres thèmes,\n"
"  les réglages de DankMaterialShell et la liste des applications installées.\n"
"  hardware.json n'est pas inclus : chaque ordinateur détecte le sien.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor backup\n"
"    maxor backup ~/Documents\n"
"    maxor backup --list copia.tar.gz"

#. help.restore
msgctxt "help.restore"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor restore <file> [--apps] [-y]\n"
"\n"
"  Brings a backup back: profiles, themes, shell settings and the theme in use.\n"
"  --apps also installs the apps in the backup. Nothing existing is overwritten\n"
"  except the shell settings (a copy is kept next to them).\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz --apps -y"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor restore <fichier> [--apps] [-y]\n"
"\n"
"  Restaure une sauvegarde : profils, thèmes, réglages du shell et thème en cours.\n"
"  --apps installe aussi les applications de la sauvegarde. Rien d'existant n'est écrasé\n"
"  sauf les réglages du shell (une copie est gardée à côté).\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz\n"
"    maxor restore copia.tar.gz --apps -y"

#. help.logs
msgctxt "help.logs"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor logs [--last | --path]\n"
"\n"
"  (none)    last 40 lines of the log\n"
"  --last    details of the last failure\n"
"  --path    path of the log file\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor logs --last"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor logs [--last | --path]\n"
"\n"
"  (rien)    les 40 dernières lignes du journal\n"
"  --last    détails de la dernière panne\n"
"  --path    chemin du fichier journal\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor logs --last"

#. help.debug
msgctxt "help.debug"
msgid ""
"Usage: maxor debug\n"
"\n"
"  Writes maxor-debug-<date>.txt here with version, hardware, doctor and log.\n"
"  Review it before sharing.\n"
"\n"
"  Examples:\n"
"    maxor debug"
msgstr ""
"Usage : maxor debug\n"
"\n"
"  Écrit ici maxor-debug-<date>.txt avec la version, le matériel, doctor et le journal.\n"
"  Relisez-le avant de le partager.\n"
"\n"
"  Exemples :\n"
"    maxor debug"

